Chapter: SpirvGpuProbe

 A GPU compute kernel in the shared PTX/SPIR-V convention: the last
 parameter, gid, is the global invocation index; the earlier parameters
 are per-element inputs read from storage buffers; the return is the
 per-element output written back. Two f64 inputs exercise the general
 multi-buffer path, not just a single-input kernel.

Section: Kernel

  gpu-scale : Real, Real, Integer -> Real
  gpu-scale (x) (k) (gid) =
   x * k + 1.0
